documentation
text

	^ 'Text model: String>>asRopedText answers a BlRopedText (subclass of BlText, see Bloc-Text-Rope). BlText offers a fluent styling API on the text instance: fontSize: 24, fontName: Microsoft YaHei, foreground: Color red, bold, italic, weight:, background:, attributes: aCollection, attribute: from: to:, and range styling via (text from: 1 to: 2) fontName: .... Render it with BlTextElement new text: aBlText, or with aBlText asElement. BlTextElement supports highlighting (highlightCategory:with:), selection and measurement strategies. IMPORTANT: the font setter is fontName:, there is no fontFamilyName:. For CJK glyphs on Windows name a font that actually contains them, e.g. Microsoft YaHei or SimSun, otherwise the platform default font may miss the glyphs. BlText announces changes (when:do:) and is the data holder: never conflate the text model with its visual element.'